WEBVTT

00:00:00.990 --> 00:00:02.950
The Digital World,

00:00:02.950 --> 00:00:06.080
a world inhabited by unusual 
creatures called Digimon.

00:00:06.080 --> 00:00:09.950
It has been conquered 
by the evil Bagra Army

00:00:09.950 --> 00:00:14.570
and divided into seven Kingdoms 
ruled by seven Death Generals.

00:00:15.200 --> 00:00:18.280
Taiki Kudou has leapt 
into these seven Kingdoms

00:00:18.280 --> 00:00:22.050
along with his partner, 
Shoutmon, to save the Digimon.

00:00:22.590 --> 00:00:25.660
This is the story of the 
friendship and adventures

00:00:25.660 --> 00:00:28.540
shared by Taiki, his friends, 
and the Digimon.

00:01:50.850 --> 00:01:53.490
The sixth Kingdom, Canyon Land,

00:01:53.490 --> 00:01:55.390
is ruled by the Death General Gravimon.

00:01:56.280 --> 00:02:00.830
Kiriha thought he could obtain ultimate 
strength by defeating his friends,

00:02:00.830 --> 00:02:02.520
and launched an attack on us,

00:02:03.030 --> 00:02:06.400
but then he realized that friends 
were what he really wanted.

00:02:07.170 --> 00:02:09.870
Our friendship bound us 
tighter than ever before,

00:02:09.870 --> 00:02:13.280
and at last, X7 was born!

00:02:15.580 --> 00:02:24.140
<b>X7 of Friendship!</b>

00:02:16.180 --> 00:02:24.140
<b>The Epic Battle with Gravimon!!</b>

00:02:17.770 --> 00:02:19.740
X7 of Friendship!

00:02:19.740 --> 00:02:22.070
The Epic Battle with Gravimon!!

00:02:25.410 --> 00:02:28.930
Shoutmon X7!

00:02:28.930 --> 00:02:30.780
X7, you say?

00:02:41.960 --> 00:02:43.250
Why, you!

00:02:43.250 --> 00:02:45.280
Octa Gravity!

00:02:47.820 --> 00:02:49.220
The gravity...

00:02:49.220 --> 00:02:50.780
Darn it...

00:02:50.780 --> 00:02:53.420
You think this can beat me?!

00:02:55.290 --> 00:02:56.190
What?!

00:02:57.330 --> 00:03:00.560
X7! Show him what our bond can do!

00:03:11.340 --> 00:03:12.900
S-So strong!

00:03:12.900 --> 00:03:14.740
How do you have so much power?

00:03:14.740 --> 00:03:18.060
This is the true strength that 
Deckerdramon talked about!

00:03:21.870 --> 00:03:23.510
Here comes the final blow!

00:03:25.230 --> 00:03:28.720
Xros Burning Rocker!

00:03:35.790 --> 00:03:39.500
H-How dare you?!

00:03:41.670 --> 00:03:44.670
Did you see that? That was X7's power!

00:03:44.670 --> 00:03:45.790
We did it!

00:03:45.790 --> 00:03:46.690
Yeah!

00:03:47.370 --> 00:03:48.570
But...

00:03:51.840 --> 00:03:52.880
Kiriha...

00:03:59.140 --> 00:04:01.010
Deckerdramon...

00:04:01.010 --> 00:04:02.450
It's my fault...

00:04:03.150 --> 00:04:04.440
Kiriha...

00:04:09.120 --> 00:04:10.350
What's wrong?

00:04:10.930 --> 00:04:12.510
I guess I got hurt a little.

00:04:13.140 --> 00:04:14.520
It's swollen!

00:04:14.520 --> 00:04:17.340
Yeah, but it doesn't hurt that much.

00:04:17.340 --> 00:04:19.460
Taiki, something's not right.

00:04:20.760 --> 00:04:23.430
The path to the next 
Kingdom isn't appearing.

00:04:23.430 --> 00:04:25.140
He's right.

00:04:25.140 --> 00:04:27.720
I thought we defeated the Death General,

00:04:27.720 --> 00:04:30.010
but the flag isn't changing...

00:04:30.900 --> 00:04:33.420
Reload, Monitamons!

00:04:35.050 --> 00:04:36.540
DigiXros!

00:04:37.160 --> 00:04:38.720
DigiXros!

00:04:45.200 --> 00:04:47.940
Hi-VisionMonitamon!

00:04:49.170 --> 00:04:50.910
If we go to Gravimon's castle,

00:04:50.910 --> 00:04:52.780
we might be able to 
find something there.

00:04:52.780 --> 00:04:53.910
Go and look.

00:04:53.910 --> 00:04:55.270
Understood.

00:04:55.880 --> 00:04:58.110
Enemies can find us too easily here.

00:04:58.110 --> 00:05:00.240
Let's get somewhere safe 
and treat that arm, Taiki.

00:05:00.240 --> 00:05:01.930
Okay. Thanks.

00:05:23.890 --> 00:05:26.770
That's a rather suspicious door!

00:05:33.300 --> 00:05:35.000
That's suspicious, too.

00:05:42.540 --> 00:05:45.960
It appears Xros Heart is still 
hiding somewhere in the vicinity.

00:05:59.670 --> 00:06:01.500
Darn that X7.

00:06:01.500 --> 00:06:04.480
Even I was in a pinch there.

00:06:04.480 --> 00:06:07.690
But unfortunately for them, 
I can regenerate,

00:06:07.690 --> 00:06:10.050
as long as my core is unharmed.

00:06:18.180 --> 00:06:19.560
Gravimon has...

00:06:19.560 --> 00:06:21.110
Regenerated?

00:06:22.060 --> 00:06:24.900
What does he mean? What is his core?

00:06:24.900 --> 00:06:26.660
I don't know.

00:06:26.660 --> 00:06:30.410
But, while on the subject, 
I saw a strange room earlier.

00:06:30.410 --> 00:06:31.570
A room?

00:06:32.820 --> 00:06:34.870
What happened, Hi-VisionMonitamon?

00:06:36.320 --> 00:06:37.180
A spy, eh?

00:06:37.930 --> 00:06:40.210
Very clever, Xros Heart.

00:06:40.210 --> 00:06:41.730
I'll be keeping him.

00:06:41.730 --> 00:06:44.110
If you want him back, 
come to the castle.

00:06:44.110 --> 00:06:47.820
And this time, 
Lord Gravimon will defeat X7.

00:06:49.720 --> 00:06:51.530
Hi-VisionMonitamon!

00:06:52.830 --> 00:06:55.090
Kiriha was a disappointment,

00:06:55.090 --> 00:06:57.520
but X7's power is the real deal.

00:06:57.520 --> 00:06:59.470
I would love to have that power.

00:06:59.470 --> 00:07:01.700
X7?

00:07:01.700 --> 00:07:04.390
But will threatening them with a hostage

00:07:04.390 --> 00:07:06.770
really be enough to 
make Taiki Kudou obey?

00:07:06.770 --> 00:07:08.760
The hostage is no more than bait.

00:07:08.760 --> 00:07:11.270
We only need to defeat X7.

00:07:11.920 --> 00:07:15.010
It is impossible for them to defeat me.

00:07:15.010 --> 00:07:19.120
They have no choice but 
to surrender to me.

00:07:19.720 --> 00:07:23.280
I never thought Gravimon 
could regenerate.

00:07:23.280 --> 00:07:25.870
He said something about a core.

00:07:25.870 --> 00:07:27.830
You think that's his weakness?

00:07:27.830 --> 00:07:31.530
But our first priority now is 
rescuing Hi-VisionMonitamon.

00:07:31.530 --> 00:07:32.560
Let's make a plan.

00:07:32.560 --> 00:07:34.260
What kind of plan?

00:07:34.260 --> 00:07:36.430
We'll all think of one together.

00:07:36.430 --> 00:07:39.390
Three breads are better 
than one, right?

00:07:39.390 --> 00:07:41.150
That's "three heads."

00:07:41.150 --> 00:07:42.540
Huh? It is?

00:07:42.540 --> 00:07:43.980
Taiki.

00:07:44.740 --> 00:07:48.240
You call me a friend even 
after I betrayed you.

00:07:48.240 --> 00:07:50.250
I'm truly grateful.

00:07:57.420 --> 00:07:59.510
Of course I would! That's obvious!

00:08:01.870 --> 00:08:03.850
Obvious, huh?

00:08:05.160 --> 00:08:07.370
You really are something.

00:08:07.370 --> 00:08:09.090
So you finally get it?

00:08:09.090 --> 00:08:12.290
My General is the best 
in the Digital World!

00:08:12.810 --> 00:08:14.750
Well, that might be an exaggeration.

00:08:14.750 --> 00:08:15.970
What?!

00:08:18.210 --> 00:08:20.150
Whoa! He laughed!

00:08:20.670 --> 00:08:23.890
I've never seen Kiriha laugh before!

00:08:23.890 --> 00:08:25.830
Now that you mention it, 
I'm not sure I have, either.

00:08:29.850 --> 00:08:31.860
M-More importantly!

00:08:31.860 --> 00:08:33.210
Let's come up with a plan!

00:08:34.440 --> 00:08:36.960
Yeah, you're right.

00:08:36.960 --> 00:08:39.690
At any rate, let's save 
Hi-VisionMonitamon

00:08:39.690 --> 00:08:41.900
and defeat Gravimon next time.

00:08:41.900 --> 00:08:44.540
Then we head for the 
seventh and final Kingdom.

00:08:45.250 --> 00:08:46.100
Right!

00:08:46.740 --> 00:08:47.740
Yes!

00:08:48.370 --> 00:08:49.370
Yeah!

00:08:50.640 --> 00:08:53.360
<i>Deckerdramon, watch me.</i>

00:08:53.360 --> 00:08:56.810
<i>I will fight to the end with my friends.</i>

00:09:07.430 --> 00:09:12.530
It will be interesting to see how X7 
approaches through this high security.

00:09:12.910 --> 00:09:13.630
Is that...

00:09:16.170 --> 00:09:18.180
Taiki Kudou?!

00:09:18.180 --> 00:09:20.640
I'll show you the ace up our sleeve.

00:09:20.640 --> 00:09:22.870
H-Here comes X7!

00:09:28.600 --> 00:09:30.010
Reload!

00:09:35.190 --> 00:09:36.120
Cutemon!

00:09:37.920 --> 00:09:38.860
Dondokomon!

00:09:40.730 --> 00:09:41.390
Knightmon!

00:09:41.390 --> 00:09:42.580
Knight!

00:09:42.580 --> 00:09:43.630
PawnChessmons!

00:09:43.630 --> 00:09:45.100
Pawn!

00:09:45.100 --> 00:09:45.930
Bastemon!

00:09:47.800 --> 00:09:48.730
ChibiKamemon!

00:09:50.570 --> 00:09:51.970
Jijimon!

00:09:55.270 --> 00:09:57.030
DigiXros!

00:09:57.570 --> 00:09:59.310
DigiXros!

00:10:03.950 --> 00:10:06.380
G-Cutemon!

00:10:11.530 --> 00:10:13.330
That's X7?!

00:10:13.330 --> 00:10:14.880
But something's different...

00:10:16.290 --> 00:10:19.330
Greatest Sonic Wave!

00:10:27.920 --> 00:10:28.810
What?!

00:10:29.370 --> 00:10:30.960
Very funny.

00:10:30.960 --> 00:10:33.950
Who knew they had a fighter like this?

00:10:33.950 --> 00:10:36.100
<i>But they can't fool me.</i>

00:10:36.100 --> 00:10:37.480
<i>This is a decoy.</i>

00:10:37.480 --> 00:10:40.620
<i>They're trying to draw 
our forces to them...</i>

00:10:40.620 --> 00:10:44.160
While they come here!

00:10:45.850 --> 00:10:48.260
Saw through us, did he?

00:10:49.960 --> 00:10:53.110
Gravimon, give Hi-VisionMonitamon 
back to us.

00:10:53.110 --> 00:10:56.700
Then I challenge you. 
Let's finish what we started.

00:10:56.700 --> 00:10:59.770
If X7 wins, I'll return the hostage.

00:10:59.770 --> 00:11:03.770
But when X7 loses, 
he will become my servant.

00:11:05.900 --> 00:11:07.020
Fine.

00:11:07.020 --> 00:11:07.910
Taiki!

00:11:07.910 --> 00:11:09.660
Good answer.

00:11:20.260 --> 00:11:22.590
Is there something in there?

00:11:22.590 --> 00:11:25.460
Yes. The hostage from 
Xros Heart is in here.

00:11:25.460 --> 00:11:27.960
I see. Keep up the good work.

00:11:27.960 --> 00:11:29.530
U-Um...

00:11:29.530 --> 00:11:31.370
Snake Punch!

00:11:32.700 --> 00:11:38.490
We save Hi-VisionMonitamon while Taiki's 
team is diverting the enemy's attention!

00:11:38.490 --> 00:11:41.650
Then we destroy Gravimon's 
core so he can't regenerate!

00:11:42.130 --> 00:11:43.610
I can't let you do that.

00:11:45.150 --> 00:11:48.100
So even X7 is a decoy?

00:11:48.100 --> 00:11:51.260
But Lord Gravimon has already 
seen through your plan.

00:11:52.390 --> 00:11:54.460
I won't let you pass.

00:11:55.590 --> 00:11:57.200
Take this!

00:11:59.060 --> 00:12:00.030
He's not dodging?

00:12:05.700 --> 00:12:08.210
I have no need to dodge.

00:12:08.660 --> 00:12:10.940
He's totally back to normal...

00:12:15.710 --> 00:12:18.670
Nene! Leave this to me and go on ahead!

00:12:18.670 --> 00:12:19.950
Counting on you!

00:12:19.950 --> 00:12:21.450
Fire!

00:12:24.190 --> 00:12:27.630
Ouch!

00:12:28.130 --> 00:12:29.010
It's working!

00:12:29.010 --> 00:12:30.900
He can't take a hit!

00:12:31.350 --> 00:12:33.670
The disguise is lost, huh?

00:12:33.990 --> 00:12:37.040
We've got to buy just 
a little more time!

00:12:39.980 --> 00:12:41.330
Miss Nene!

00:12:41.330 --> 00:12:43.470
I'm glad you're okay, 
Hi-VisionMonitamon!

00:12:43.470 --> 00:12:47.630
I know I just freed you, but can you 
take me to that room you saw now?

00:12:47.630 --> 00:12:49.080
Leave it to me!

00:12:49.080 --> 00:12:51.550
Death Divider!

00:12:53.660 --> 00:12:56.040
It's probably useless, 
but I'll ask anyway.

00:12:56.040 --> 00:12:57.830
What is Gravimon's core?

00:12:57.830 --> 00:12:58.720
Where is it?

00:12:58.720 --> 00:12:59.910
I don't know.

00:13:00.390 --> 00:13:02.700
Even if you knew,

00:13:02.700 --> 00:13:05.600
you could never defeat Lord Gravimon.

00:13:05.600 --> 00:13:07.220
What do you mean?

00:13:09.100 --> 00:13:13.550
You should regret your change of heart.

00:13:19.150 --> 00:13:20.280
G-Cutemon!

00:13:20.280 --> 00:13:22.310
I-I'm done for...

00:13:22.310 --> 00:13:24.260
I can't hold out any longer!

00:13:26.240 --> 00:13:28.040
Hey, wait for us!

00:13:28.040 --> 00:13:30.860
Don't leave us behind!

00:13:30.860 --> 00:13:32.800
Sorry, Taiki.

00:13:32.800 --> 00:13:34.560
We've reached our limit here.

00:13:36.030 --> 00:13:37.710
X7, I'm counting on you!

00:13:38.200 --> 00:13:40.830
Xros Burning Rocker!

00:13:51.510 --> 00:13:52.710
How about now?

00:14:03.720 --> 00:14:04.890
It didn't work.

00:14:05.330 --> 00:14:06.520
<i>It's no use!</i>

00:14:06.520 --> 00:14:08.790
<i>Until we stop his regeneration, 
we can't defeat him!</i>

00:14:09.180 --> 00:14:12.360
<i>All we can do now is rely on the 
info we get from Nene and Kiriha!</i>

00:14:12.760 --> 00:14:16.550
The strange door is just 
around that corner!

00:14:16.550 --> 00:14:17.570
That's where the core is?

00:14:18.120 --> 00:14:19.140
There it is!

00:14:23.500 --> 00:14:24.180
What is this?

00:14:24.670 --> 00:14:27.050
We were wrong. It's just a treasury.

00:14:27.050 --> 00:14:28.390
Miss Nene!

00:14:28.390 --> 00:14:30.110
Monitamon! What have you found?

00:14:30.110 --> 00:14:33.000
Nothing. We searched the whole castle,

00:14:33.000 --> 00:14:35.370
but there's nothing 
that looks like a core.

00:14:35.370 --> 00:14:36.150
No...

00:14:36.150 --> 00:14:38.890
Does that mean our 
calculations were wrong?

00:14:39.750 --> 00:14:42.090
If this keeps up, 
Taiki's team is in trouble!

00:14:42.700 --> 00:14:44.950
The soldiers are coming back!

00:14:46.200 --> 00:14:49.070
Now it's time for me to have some fun.

00:14:49.070 --> 00:14:50.940
DigiXros!

00:14:59.530 --> 00:15:02.710
Gravimon Darkness Mode!

00:15:06.450 --> 00:15:07.520
X7!

00:15:12.680 --> 00:15:15.190
Did you see that power?

00:15:18.550 --> 00:15:20.000
Cyberdramon!

00:15:20.000 --> 00:15:21.460
Taiki!

00:15:21.460 --> 00:15:22.930
You're all okay?

00:15:24.970 --> 00:15:28.200
Taiki, let me finish Gravimon.

00:15:28.200 --> 00:15:28.840
Kiriha...

00:15:29.170 --> 00:15:33.010
Kiriha, eh? Well, it's all the same, 
no matter who fights me.

00:15:33.320 --> 00:15:35.570
If you're talking about 
your ability to regenerate,

00:15:35.570 --> 00:15:37.450
I just have to crush you 
into so many pieces,

00:15:37.450 --> 00:15:38.580
you won't get the chance!

00:15:38.580 --> 00:15:40.050
And can you do that?

00:15:40.050 --> 00:15:41.750
Shut up! Let's go!

00:15:43.990 --> 00:15:44.790
What?!

00:15:45.980 --> 00:15:47.370
I'm over here.

00:15:50.140 --> 00:15:52.330
My speed is amazing, too!

00:15:52.330 --> 00:15:55.030
Darn it! X7, we're going this way!

00:16:04.480 --> 00:16:05.080
Kiriha!

00:16:07.110 --> 00:16:08.310
Darn it...

00:16:08.310 --> 00:16:12.220
What do you say now? 
Your tactics are no match for me!

00:16:12.220 --> 00:16:13.620
I'm not done yet!

00:16:16.490 --> 00:16:18.090
What's wrong, Kiriha?

00:16:19.360 --> 00:16:23.630
I can see right through the short 
foresight of such an impertinent boy!

00:16:24.260 --> 00:16:26.400
High Gravity Pressure!

00:16:30.900 --> 00:16:32.630
Do you get it now?

00:16:32.630 --> 00:16:35.000
Whether I can regenerate or not,

00:16:35.000 --> 00:16:37.340
you can never beat me!

00:16:38.440 --> 00:16:39.710
Kiriha!

00:16:41.810 --> 00:16:43.310
Serves you right.

00:16:48.290 --> 00:16:50.490
Kiriha! X7!

00:16:52.660 --> 00:16:56.110
Let me tell you something 
helpful, Kiriha.

00:16:56.110 --> 00:16:59.130
There is but one way to defeat me.

00:16:59.130 --> 00:17:00.570
What?

00:17:00.570 --> 00:17:03.130
By killing Taiki Kudou.

00:17:04.800 --> 00:17:08.690
You still insist on telling me that?

00:17:08.690 --> 00:17:11.360
It's the truth. Look.

00:17:13.170 --> 00:17:14.610
Taiki!

00:17:15.720 --> 00:17:17.640
What did you do to Taiki?!

00:17:17.640 --> 00:17:21.720
As long as the core that 
is my heart exists,

00:17:21.720 --> 00:17:23.990
I can regenerate infinitely.

00:17:23.990 --> 00:17:28.150
And that core moves around at my will.

00:17:28.150 --> 00:17:29.360
It moves?

00:17:30.060 --> 00:17:31.030
It can't be!

00:17:36.500 --> 00:17:40.070
When I was attacked in our last battle,

00:17:40.070 --> 00:17:43.570
I quickly sent my core 
into Taiki Kudou's arm.

00:17:49.360 --> 00:17:50.390
Taiki...

00:17:50.390 --> 00:17:50.880
Taiki!

00:17:51.430 --> 00:17:53.050
Well, what's the problem?

00:17:53.050 --> 00:17:55.270
If you kill Taiki Kudou, 
my core also dies,

00:17:55.270 --> 00:17:57.260
and you can defeat me.

00:17:58.170 --> 00:18:01.230
Didn't you say that you 
wanted ultimate strength

00:18:01.230 --> 00:18:04.300
even if it meant 
sacrificing your friends?

00:18:04.830 --> 00:18:07.270
Taiki! Rip that thing out!

00:18:07.270 --> 00:18:08.430
That's impossible.

00:18:08.430 --> 00:18:11.270
My core has already merged with him.

00:18:11.560 --> 00:18:14.210
If you want to defeat me and 
move to the next Kingdom,

00:18:14.210 --> 00:18:16.710
you must kill Taiki Kudou.

00:18:17.210 --> 00:18:20.100
Kill... Taiki?

00:18:21.310 --> 00:18:22.540
Ridiculous!

00:18:22.540 --> 00:18:23.210
That's dirty!

00:18:24.560 --> 00:18:27.820
If we don't defeat Gravimon, 
we can't get to the last Kingdom.

00:18:28.760 --> 00:18:31.660
And we can't defeat Bagramon.

00:18:38.360 --> 00:18:40.980
Kiriha, you can't...

00:18:43.230 --> 00:18:45.530
<i>I trust Kiriha.</i>

00:18:45.530 --> 00:18:47.520
<i>He wouldn't do something like that.</i>

00:18:48.090 --> 00:18:50.110
<i>I believe Kiriha is our friend.</i>

00:18:50.110 --> 00:18:51.950
<i>I'll fight with him.</i>

00:18:51.950 --> 00:18:54.180
<i>Of course I would! That's obvious!</i>

00:19:04.740 --> 00:19:07.090
You know I can't do that.

00:19:09.390 --> 00:19:11.590
I surrender, Gravimon.

00:19:12.230 --> 00:19:13.800
Kiriha, no!

00:19:13.800 --> 00:19:17.040
Taiki... I have no other options.

00:19:17.040 --> 00:19:19.160
What a fool.

00:19:19.160 --> 00:19:23.470
You choose the path of 
weakness and accept defeat?

00:19:23.770 --> 00:19:26.620
No! Kiriha is not weak!

00:19:26.620 --> 00:19:28.010
Forget it, Taiki.

00:19:29.540 --> 00:19:34.210
Gravimon! I don't need the 
strength you speak of anymore!

00:19:34.210 --> 00:19:36.450
If you want to call me weak, go ahead!

00:19:36.450 --> 00:19:37.900
How noble.

00:19:37.900 --> 00:19:41.850
Then I'll take your Xros Loader 
as a sign of your surrender.

00:19:41.850 --> 00:19:42.630
Kiriha!

00:19:42.630 --> 00:19:43.970
It's all right.

00:19:43.970 --> 00:19:47.530
Even if I surrender now, 
I can turn the tables again someday.

00:19:48.190 --> 00:19:49.880
As long as you're around.

00:19:54.250 --> 00:19:56.040
Here! Take it!

00:19:56.040 --> 00:19:58.210
<i>Kiriha Aonuma...</i>

00:19:58.210 --> 00:20:01.280
<i>A foolish loser who 
failed to become strong.</i>

00:20:01.570 --> 00:20:05.350
<i>But he doesn't have the 
empty eyes of a loser.</i>

00:20:06.380 --> 00:20:08.020
I don't like this deal.

00:20:08.020 --> 00:20:12.060
I need you to realize 
what a fool you are.

00:20:13.930 --> 00:20:14.960
Disappear!

00:20:23.770 --> 00:20:25.240
<i>Taiki!</i>

00:20:25.240 --> 00:20:25.940
What?!

00:20:26.240 --> 00:20:29.310
<i>Gravimon, if I die, so do you!</i>

00:20:33.970 --> 00:20:35.710
Core! Leave him!

00:20:40.490 --> 00:20:42.200
You're not getting away!

00:20:48.360 --> 00:20:49.560
They did it!

00:20:55.400 --> 00:20:58.230
Y-You... Taiki Kudou!

00:20:58.230 --> 00:21:01.710
I never thought you'd 
dive in front of him!

00:21:01.710 --> 00:21:06.610
Gravimon, our strength isn't the kind 
that makes sacrifices of our friends.

00:21:06.610 --> 00:21:08.850
It's the strength to 
protect our friends!

00:21:12.430 --> 00:21:15.190
No!

00:21:19.720 --> 00:21:22.560
Honestly, Taiki, could 
you be any more reckless?

00:21:22.560 --> 00:21:26.810
He's right! Even if you 
did it to save him...

00:21:26.810 --> 00:21:28.800
Yeah, but...

00:21:28.800 --> 00:21:30.650
I thought if I was about to die,

00:21:30.650 --> 00:21:33.400
maybe the core would come out.

00:21:35.850 --> 00:21:37.740
What are we going to do with you?

00:21:37.740 --> 00:21:41.890
Kiriha, it's great that you 
got to avenge Deckerdramon!

00:21:42.790 --> 00:21:45.620
Yeah. But it's not over yet.

00:21:45.620 --> 00:21:46.920
You got that right!

00:21:46.920 --> 00:21:49.050
Come on, let's head 
for the next Kingdom!

00:21:49.050 --> 00:21:49.690
Yeah!

00:21:51.560 --> 00:21:54.160
<i>Once we defeat the last Death General,</i>

00:21:54.160 --> 00:21:55.660
<i>it's time for the final showdown.</i>

00:21:56.230 --> 00:21:59.130
Watch over me, Deckerdramon.

00:21:59.900 --> 00:22:02.700
He's watching. I know it.

00:22:07.570 --> 00:22:09.740
<b>To Be Continued</b>

00:22:09.740 --> 00:22:13.280
<b>Digimon Data Collection</b>

00:22:10.740 --> 00:22:13.280
Digimon Data Collection!

00:22:13.280 --> 00:22:17.220
<b>Listen to the Digimon's melody!</b>

00:22:13.840 --> 00:22:17.220
Listen to the melody of 
this Digimon I caught!

00:22:14.220 --> 00:22:15.220
<b>Melody starts in 3 seconds.</b>

00:22:15.220 --> 00:22:16.220
<b>Melody starts in 2 seconds.</b>

00:22:16.220 --> 00:22:17.220
<b>Melody starts in 1 second.</b>

00:22:19.880 --> 00:22:34.100
<b>[Type]</b>

00:22:22.220 --> 00:22:39.640
<b>Holy Beast Type</b>

00:22:23.120 --> 00:22:34.100
<b>[Attacks]</b>

00:22:24.560 --> 00:22:27.030
<b>Curse of Queen  
Rosetta Stone</b>

00:22:27.030 --> 00:22:39.640
<b>Curse of Quee  
Rosetta Stone</b>

00:22:27.190 --> 00:22:28.710
Nefertimon.

00:22:28.710 --> 00:22:33.990
Her Curse of Queen attack shoots a 
superheated beam from her headdress.

00:22:33.990 --> 00:22:36.060
What a sweet-looking kitty!

00:22:36.060 --> 00:22:37.180
Here, kitty!

00:22:37.180 --> 00:22:39.640
She's gonna scratch you!

00:22:41.540 --> 00:22:43.310
We're finally heading 
for the last Kingdom!

00:22:43.310 --> 00:22:47.010
What?! A Death General 
with a just heart?!

00:22:47.010 --> 00:22:48.110
I am Apollomon.

00:22:48.110 --> 00:22:51.520
Fight with me so we can 
defeat Bagramon together!

00:22:51.520 --> 00:22:52.520
Digimon Xros Wars!

00:22:52.520 --> 00:22:54.470
<b>The Final Kingdom,</b>

00:22:52.520 --> 00:22:54.470
<b>Bright Land of the Shining Sun</b>

00:22:52.520 --> 00:22:54.520
You can't turn your back 
on the next one, either!
